  "description": "The grand world with plants that evolve (living plants, step 1). Every patch of ground carries its own plant genome: a chemistry (which animals digest best, by their palate gene), the time of year it grows best and the temperature it likes. Ground eaten bare is reseeded from neighbouring plants standing tall, and every seed mutates a little. It starts as the grand world's three kinds. Watch the overlays Kinds of plant (chemistry spreads from three kinds into many) and Plant warmth (compare with Temperature: cold places come to grow cold-loving plants), and color the dots by Palate. In a first 40,000-tick run plants' best temperature went from barely following the local temperature (correlation 0.10) to clearly following it (0.60), and the three chemistries spread into about eight.",
